Pilot additions for sdd-bench on Compass 8.x (local lab patch, never pushed)

Apply after compass-harness-multi-round.patch, to evals/harness.py at the
Compass tag the pilot measures:

    patch -p1 < compass-harness-multi-round.patch
    patch -p1 < compass-harness-pilot.patch

It adds two things the multi-round runner lacks:

- SDD_KEEP_WORKSPACE=<dir> copies each run's repository, with .git and
  .compass/, to <dir>/<scenario>-<condition>-<run>/ when the session ends
  and before the hidden tests are copied in, so tools/check_record.py can
  read it.
- The runner answers Compass approval requests as the person would, at a
  terminal. Compass 8.x records an approval only from a typed
  /compass:approve (refused in a `claude -p` session, whose
  CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT is sdk-cli) or from `compass evidence approve`
  with a terminal on standard input. Before the model approver is asked,
  the runner runs that verb under a pseudo-terminal for every file in
  .compass/work/*/approval-requests/pending/, as approver
  sdd-bench-approver, role owner, then tells the session it approved.

